## Method Hiding

--> Method Hiding happens when a static method in the Child class has the same name and parameters as a static method in the parent class
--> in this case the method in the child class hides the method in the Parent class.
E.g :- SChool or tution :-> Both give homework using the same method name but the work in different it depends on where you are calling from school or tution

public class Parent {
	static void display1()
	{
		System.out.println("inside parent display 1");
	}
	static void display2()
	{
		System.out.println("inside parent display 2");
	}
	
}
public class Child extends Parent{
	static void display2()
	{
		System.out.println("inside child display 2");
	}
}
public class Main {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Parent pr1 = new Parent();
		pr1.display2();
		pr1.display2();
		Child ch = new Child();
		ch.display1();
		ch.display2();
		Parent pr2 = new Parent();
		pr2.display1();
		pr2.display2();
	}
}
